          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. Seizure onset occurred at 10 years of age. Current seizure frequency is approximately five seizures per week.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Oxcarbazepine\n- Perampanel\n- Lacosamide\n\nSeizure Burden:\nFocal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures occur approximately five times per week despite the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. The etiology is genetic, caused by an SCN1A c.5734C>T variant.\n\nPlan:\nContinue the current antiseizure medications: oxcarbazepine, perampanel, and lacosamide. Continue monitoring seizure frequency and treatment response.",
